//The test template for page based change history
//All changes should be cleared on an intentional app/page close. If the app crashes or something, changes should stay there.
//And thus, changes should still be stored in local storage. 
//When the app launches it should look for a file called "crash_status" in its executing directory.
//The app then reads the contents of that file and if its a '0' that means the app didn't crash unexpectedly.
//If its a '1' that means the app was actively running before it was suddenly stopped without a proper close sequence.
//This is kind of like what windows does with USB drives and their 'dirty bit'.
//page histories should be stored inside of the pagestates individually
{
    //...PageState data
    "change_history": [
        {
            "node_type": "Group",
            "node_id": "Group One",
            "changed_property": "Offsets_Position_X",
            "new_value": 123,
            "original_value": 0
        }
    ]
}